2c:["$","p",null,{"children":["The path segment after ",["$","code",null,{"children":"scheduler/"}]," is the scheduler's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"name"}]," from the\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"schedulers"}]," list, not a REAPI instance name. The endpoint only exists on a\nlistener with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"admin: {}"}]," in its services (the shipped Kubernetes config has\nnone); put it on the worker-API listener. It has no authentication; reach it\nover a private path only. See\n",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"/operate/security-hardening#the-admin-endpoint-has-no-authentication","children":"Security hardening"}],"."]}]
